cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Governance-Playbook
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as part of the SimpleAct AI Governance Framework."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: SimpleAct-Compliance
repository-code: "https://github.com/SimpleAct-Compliance/simpleact-ai-governance-playbook"
license: MIT
abstract: "Who decides, who reviews, who escalates — and who has the hours for it. An operating model for AI governance under Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 built around three roles defined by what each may not do, a go-live gate that asks for effectiveness rather than intent, and four escalation triggers including two that no common model contains: a finding deferred a third time, and an oversight metric falling towards zero. Both describe decisions nobody has spoken aloud."
keywords:
  - EU AI Act
  - AI governance
  - accountability
  - go-live gate
  - escalation
  - delegation
  - review cadence
  - Article 14
  - Article 25
  - SimpleAct
